{"summary":"Reviewed the three amendments against the current budget-tracking code. The runtime `Option<BudgetLedger>` gating satisfies the stated zero-cost-when-disabled requirement, and the missing oxygen tick guard is not a correctness bug because the implementation tracks dissolved oxygen diagnostically rather than as a conserved whole-system oxygen inventory. The real remaining weakness is the aggregate microbe assertion in the nitrogen helper test, which can miss per-component mapping mistakes even though label coverage is checked elsewhere.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-10-12259602","decision":"reject","rationale":"The implementation already records oxygen deltas in the ledger: ordinary stages pick up dissolved-oxygen changes through `BudgetSnapshot::from_state`, and the dissolved-oxygen and water-change paths return explicit oxygen budgets. What it does not do is apply an N/C-style conservation guard to oxygen, and that is appropriate because `BudgetTotals::oxygen_mg` is only dissolved O2, not a closed total-oxygen inventory across all modeled compounds. Closed ticks can legitimately change DO through respiration, photosynthesis, and reaeration, so a near-zero residual guard would not be measuring a conserved quantity. A clarifying comment could help future readers, but the absence of an oxygen guard is not itself a technical defect."},{"amendment_id":"fr-10-70478168","decision":"reject","rationale":"The acceptance criterion is disjunctive: the instrumentation must either compile out or be zero-cost when not in use. The current design satisfies the second half. When `budget_ledger` is `None`, no tick record is created, `BudgetSnapshot::from_state` is not called because the `Option::map` closures are skipped, and explicit-budget systems run with `tracking = false`. The remaining overhead is only trivial branch/`Option` plumbing, not meaningful budget instrumentation work. Keeping the small helper types compiled into the crate does not amount to a failure of the stated requirement."},{"amendment_id":"fr-10-75c62b7a","decision":"accept","rationale":"`test_total_n_helper_sums_all_pools` aggregates the four microbe biomasses before applying the nitrogen conversion, so it validates only the total microbial nitrogen contribution. `test_budget_component_labels_cover_all_element_bearing_fields` checks label-set completeness, but it does not prove that each individual microbe label is wired to the correct biomass field. A copy/paste error that preserves the aggregate total while misassigning one or more per-microbe component amounts could still pass both tests. Adding explicit per-pool assertions would therefore provide real defense in depth rather than redundant coverage."}]}